body:
The [spec wording](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/web-messaging.html#dom-messageport-postmessage-options) requires that messages posted before `close()` is called on the receiving port lead to events being fired even when that would happen after the `close()` call.  This, however, is not necessarily what browsers do and is inconsistent with BroadcastChannel.

https://jsfiddle.net/c9mbo2c3/2/ is one testcase, linked when this issue was [originally raised](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1371#issue-158007487).  At that time, both Chrome and Firefox fired events for this testcase as specified.  Chrome has since changed behavior.  Perhaps https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=673526 may be related to the behavior change, but I'm not clear that it covers exactly the same scenario. 

The specified behavior is intended to be tested by ['Close in onmessage should not cancel inflight messages.'](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/3075081ac1c62e1b8eef4b46c55c8056875559fa#diff-fa635d09443e9878ada0f04681fe3311R58) but a bug in the test means that this accidentally passes regardless of behavior.  Correcting with `s/step_func_done/step_func/` shows that Webkit and Blink differ from the spec.

A variant of the existing wpt, having a shipped receiving port, times out even in Gecko due to the lost "before close" message:
```js
promise_test(async () => {
  const mc = new MessageChannel;
  // A second MessageChannel "ship"s a port from the first.
  const shipper = new MessageChannel;
  shipper.port1.postMessage(null, [mc.port2]);
  const {ports: [shipped]} = await new Promise(resolve => {
    shipper.port2.onmessage = resolve;
  });
  mc.port1.postMessage("before close");
  shipped.close();
  const {data} = await new Promise(resolve => {
    shipped.onmessage = resolve;
  });
  assert_equals(data, "before close");
}, "Inflight message should be delivered to closed shipped receiving port.");
```

| Test case                 | Blink     | Gecko              | WebKit    |
|---------------------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|
| jsfiddle                  | ["first"] | ["first","second"] | ["first"] |
| corrected existing wpt    | Timeout   | Pass               | Timeout   |
| shipped receiving port    | Timeout   | Timeout            | Timeout   |

